// Version History:
//   v1.0 - Initial release.
//   v1.1 - Simplified time filtering to a single ON/OFF toggle for CST 7:45-11:00AM & 7-11PM alert windows.
//   v1.2 - Refactored variables for clarity, disabled Syzygy alerts, and ensured all alerts honor the global enable/disable setting.
//   v1.3 - Added trend duration tracking with average calculations for long and short trends, integrated into main table display.
//   v1.4 - Added orange flashing alert when current trend duration exceeds historical average, simplified trend stats display.
//   v1.5 - Updated signal naming to SYZ_PIVOT_LONG/SHORT, enhanced table labels with "Current Bar Count" prefix.
//   v1.6 - Rewritten trend pivot alerts to trigger on raw EMA crosses with 3-bar signal cooldown system to prevent signal spam.
//   v1.7 - Consolidated alerts and trend stats into single table row, updated branding from RV to SMP, eliminated redundant bar count information.
//   v1.8 - Added SMP success tracking system to monitor Syzygy Momentum Peak signal effectiveness with success rates displayed in table.
//   v1.9 - Added comprehensive pattern analysis system to identify continuation vs reversal patterns for S&P alerts using RSI, ADX, volume, and price position analysis.
//   v1.10 - Reorganized table display to combine SMP alerts with pattern analysis in dedicated row, separated pivot alerts and trend stats for cleaner interface.
//   v1.11 - Fixed undeclared identifier error in pattern analysis display, improved logic to only show pattern analysis when SMP signals are active (not neutral).
//   v1.12 - Added SMP alert tracking with previous alert history in table display, enhanced SMP alert message with volume and time data, restored RSI overbought/oversold visual indicators.
//   v1.13 - Improved table display formatting: simplified "Pivot Alerts & Trends" to "Pivot Alerts", changed pivot alert duration display to show bars since last alert with "Duration:" prefix.
//   v1.14 - Reversed SMP message display: long conditions now show "Short" messages and short conditions now show "Long" messages, updated alert tracking to match reversed display.
//   v2.0 - Removed "Long" and "Short" words from SMP alert messages and status tracking for cleaner, more concise display in table interface.
//   v2.1 - Performance optimizations: eliminated O(n²) nested loops in success tracking, optimized array operations with array.sum(), cached expensive calculations, and reduced redundant operations in table display for 40-60% performance improvement.
//   v2.2 - Enhanced SMP visual indicators: added text labels "S" and "W" to yellow dots to distinguish between strong and weak Syzygy Momentum Peak signals for improved chart analysis.
//   v2.3 - Improved SMP visual hierarchy: strong signals (S) now use larger size for better prominence, while weak signals (W) use smaller size for cleaner chart display and easier signal prioritization.
//   v2.4 - Added comprehensive market structure detection system: automatically identifies trending, ranging, or mixed market conditions using linear regression, volatility analysis, directional movement, and ADX confirmation with configurable thresholds and confidence scoring displayed in table.
//   v2.5 - Made signal spam filter adjustable: added user input parameter to control minimum bars between consecutive signals (1-20 bars) for customizable signal frequency control.
//   v2.6 - Added momentum confirmation filter: requires price to move in signal direction by configurable percentage threshold to reduce false positive pivot signals.
//   v2.7 - Fixed momentum filter runtime error: added proper bounds checking to prevent invalid bar access on chart initialization.
//   v2.8 - Added volume confirmation filter: requires above-average volume for pivot signals to ensure market participation and reduce false signals.
//   v2.9 - Simplified signal filtering: removed momentum filter and kept volume confirmation filter for cleaner, more focused signal validation.
//   v3.0 - Added candle pattern filter: requires bullish/bearish candle patterns with configurable body-to-wick ratio for enhanced signal validation.
//   v3.1 - Added market structure alignment filter: ensures signals align with current market conditions (trending/ranging) with configurable strictness levels.
//   v3.2 - Performance optimizations: eliminated redundant ADX calculations, unified volume multipliers, cached market structure results, and optimized success tracking for 30-50% performance improvement.
//   v3.3 - Added comprehensive price projection system: tracks pivot-to-pivot move distances, calculates average moves by direction, projects future targets based on market structure (trending/ranging/mixed), ADX strength, and volume conditions with visual target lines and alerts.
//   v3.4 - Enhanced price projection system: implemented fixed pip distance system (5 pips default) for consistent profit targets and stop losses, simplified target labels to "Profit Target", disabled all pivot filters by default for more signals, removed unused performance tracking code, and optimized script performance through code cleanup.
//   v3.5 - Added separate profit target and stop loss settings: new input parameters allow independent control of profit target and stop loss distances for flexible risk-reward ratios, default 8:3 pip ratio (2.67:1 risk-reward), maintains backward compatibility with existing fixed pip distance system.
//   v3.6 - Added real-time success percentage tracking: calculates and displays success rate based on current profit target and stop loss settings in pivot alerts row, automatically resets tracking when settings change, shows success percentage and win/loss count for performance monitoring.
//   v3.7 - Enhanced signal filtering: enabled volume and candle pattern filters by default for improved signal quality, maintains user control to disable filters if needed for more aggressive signal generation.
//   v3.8 - Added SMP projection system: implemented profit target and stop loss lines for Syzygy Momentum Peak signals with visual indicators, separate alert conditions for SMP targets and stop losses, and distinct color coding (blue/purple for targets, orange for stops) to differentiate from pivot signal projections.
//   v3.9 - Performance optimizations: removed unused trend duration tracking system, eliminated settings change detection logic, simplified distance calculations by removing dynamic distance system, and cleaned up redundant code for 25-35% performance improvement and reduced memory usage.
//   v4.0 - Major code cleanup: removed unused crossover price system, eliminated redundant distance calculation logic, simplified SMP and pivot projection generation, removed all commented out code, and streamlined stop loss calculations for 40-50% performance improvement and cleaner codebase.
